sentences.l:
Yuan Si acted as his steward;
he was given grain, nine hundred;
he declined.

The Master said: “Hui —
his heart for three months does not depart from humaneness;
the others reach it for a day or a month, and that is all.”

Ji Kangzi asked: “Zhong You — can he be employed in government?”
The Master said: “Yóu is decisive;
in government, what trouble would he have?”
He said: “Ci — can he be employed in government?”
He said: “Ci sees through things;
in government, what trouble would he have?”
He said: “Qiu — can he be employed in government?”
He said: “Qiu has many skills;
in government, what trouble would he have?”

The Master said to Zixia:
“You — be a gentleman's kind of scholar;
do not be a small man's kind of scholar.”

The Master said: “From middling men up,
one can tell them of the higher things;
from middling men down,
one cannot tell them of the higher things.”

The Master said: “The wise man takes to water;
the humane man takes to mountains.
The wise man moves;
the humane man is still.
The wise man enjoys;
the humane man lasts long.”

Now the humane man:
wishing to stand himself, he sets others on their feet;
wishing to get through himself, he gets others through.
